  <text id="section-label" x="60" y="58" width="250" height="22" font="caption" color="red-risk" wrap="false">01 — THE EXECUTION GAP</text>
  <text id="title" x="60" y="104" width="900" height="58" font="heading" size="40" color="text-main" wrap="false">Linux executes commands. It does not understand intent.</text>
  <text id="intro" x="60" y="184" width="905" height="58" font="body" size="19" color="text-muted" line-height="1.35">A misunderstood command can delete files, compromise permissions, or interrupt a production service before the user has a chance to understand its consequences.</text>
  <shape id="card-one" type="rect" x="60" y="285" width="360" height="238" fill="bg-panel" stroke="hairline" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="card-one-code" x="84" y="318" width="312" height="30" font="body" size="19" color="red-risk" wrap="false">$ rm -rf project/*</text>
  <text id="card-one-title" x="84" y="376" width="285" height="28" font="heading" size="22" color="text-main">Irreversible deletion</text>
  <text id="card-one-copy" x="84" y="420" width="290" height="70" font="body" size="16" color="text-muted" line-height="1.35">Wildcards and recursive flags can remove more than the operator intended.</text>
  <shape id="card-two" type="rect" x="460" y="285" width="360" height="238" fill="bg-panel" stroke="hairline" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="card-two-code" x="484" y="318" width="312" height="30" font="body" size="19" color="amber-warn" wrap="false">$ curl … | bash</text>
  <text id="card-two-title" x="484" y="376" width="285" height="28" font="heading" size="22" color="text-main">Unreviewed execution</text>
  <text id="card-two-copy" x="484" y="420" width="288" height="70" font="body" size="16" color="text-muted" line-height="1.35">Remote code is executed before its content, source, or side effects are examined.</text>
  <shape id="card-three" type="rect" x="860" y="285" width="360" height="238" fill="bg-panel" stroke="hairline" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="card-three-code" x="884" y="318" width="312" height="30" font="body" size="19" color="red-risk" wrap="false">$ sudo rm -rf /</text>
  <text id="card-three-title" x="884" y="376" width="285" height="28" font="heading" size="22" color="text-main">System-wide damage</text>
  <text id="card-three-copy" x="884" y="420" width="282" height="70" font="body" size="16" color="text-muted" line-height="1.35">Elevated privileges turn a single dangerous action into a recovery-level incident.</text>
  <shape id="conclusion-line" type="rect" x="60" y="565" width="1160" height="58" fill="#FF4C4C18" stroke="#FF4C4C50" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="conclusion" x="84" y="582" width="1110" height="28" font="body" size="18" color="text-main" wrap="false">The missing layer is not another shell command — it is an explainable safety decision before execution.</text>
  <text id="footer-page" x="60" y="676" width="80" height="20" font="caption" color="text-muted" wrap="false">02 / 10</text>
